---
source: crates/dlin/tests/integration/cli.rs
expression: long_help(args)
---
Show a summary of the dbt project: node counts by type, edge count, variable definitions, and manifest.json freshness.

Useful for onboarding, CI logs, and feeding project context to AI agents.

Output formats:
  text (default)  Human-readable summary
  json            Structured JSON for programmatic use

Manifest freshness is checked automatically when a manifest.json is found at the default location (<project-dir>/target/manifest.json) or at the path given by --manifest-path. The check detects both files newer than the manifest (stale) and files referenced in the manifest but missing from disk (deleted), using the same logic as `dlin check-manifest`.

Usage: dlin summary [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --error-format <ERROR_FORMAT>
          Error/warning output format on stderr: text (default) or json.
          
          When json, each diagnostic is one JSON object on its own line. Every
          object has {"level":"error"|"warning"|"info","what":"...","why":...,"hint":...},
          where why and hint are either strings or null. Typed diagnostics add a
          "code" and fields of their own; for example dependency_analysis_summary
          adds counts by reason type and namespace. Read code and the typed fields,
          not the text of what, why and hint.

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable error messages (default)
          - json: Structured JSON on stderr: {"level":"...","what":"...","why":...,"hint":...}
          
          [env: DLIN_ERROR_FORMAT=]
          [default: text]

  -p, --project-dir <PROJECT_DIR>
          Path to dbt project directory
          
          [default: .]

      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          Directory for caching manifest analysis results (default: <project-dir>/.dlin_cache). Has no effect with --source sql, which has no cache
          
          [env: DLIN_CACHE_DIR=]

      --verbose
          Show the details of the model dependency analysis on stderr.
          
          By default, a command that builds the lineage graph prints at most one
          configuration warning and one dependency_analysis_summary diagnostic, which
          counts the reasons of the whole project by type and namespace. With
          --verbose it also prints one diagnostic per reason (with the node and the
          call site) and per skipped input, and the info diagnostics for default
          paths that do not exist. It changes no analysis. --quiet takes precedence.

      --no-cache
          Disable the manifest analysis cache (always re-parse the manifest, results are not saved). Has no effect with --source sql, which has no cache
          
          [env: DLIN_NO_CACHE=]

      --refresh-cache
          Discard the existing manifest analysis cache and rebuild it. Has no effect with --source sql, which has no cache
          
          [env: DLIN_REFRESH_CACHE=]

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format: text (default) or json
          
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, json]

      --source <SOURCE>
          Data source for building the lineage graph.
          
            sql (default)   Parse SQL files directly — no dbt or Python required.
                            Exposures and generic tests are detected from YAML with
                            dlin-specific IDs; use manifest mode for exact test
                            dependency resolution.
            manifest        Use dbt manifest.json for full accuracy. Requires
                            prior `dbt compile` (or `dbt run`/`dbt build`).

          Possible values:
          - sql:      Parse SQL files directly — no dbt/Python required. Exposures and generic tests are detected from YAML with dlin-specific IDs; use manifest mode for exact test dependency resolution
          - manifest: Use dbt manifest.json — full accuracy, requires prior `dbt compile`
          
          [default: sql]

      --manifest-path <MANIFEST_PATH>
          Path to manifest.json file or directory containing target/manifest.json.
          
          Default: <project-dir>/target/manifest.json

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress warning messages

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  # Quick project overview
  dlin summary

  # JSON output for AI agents
  dlin summary -o json

  # Use manifest as data source
  dlin summary --source manifest
